          "filename": "Chapel within Strata Florida abbey - geograph.org.uk - 652911.jpg",
          "caption": "Chapel within Strata Florida abbey. This is one of the six chapels at the back of the abbey complex (the second from the south to be geographically specific).  There are two blocks of three chapels, and within each block, the three chapels are side by side.  Each is a simple rectangular room with a section of elevated floor at the back (presumably where the altar was located).  The wooden roof structure is in place to protect the medieval floor tiles (652905) from the weather.",
